      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1868 the Perkiomen Branch of the Reading Railroad arrived, linking Zieglerville to broader markets and sparking modest industrial and commercial growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/zieglerville_pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 2025 Montgomery Award‑winning project restored two 19th‑century buildings—a Victorian brick home and a stone house—into an engineering firm office and a distillery, blending heritage with commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/zieglerville_pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Zieglerville lies along the historic Perkiomen and Sumneytown Turnpike, just north of Swamp Creek within the Perkiomen Creek watershed.",
